# Library Book Management App

This React app allows you to manage a library's book collection using an online database (Firebase Firestore).

## Features
- List all books
- Add new books
- Edit existing books
- Delete books

## Setup
1. Install dependencies:
   ```
   npm install
   ```
2. Set up a Firebase project at https://console.firebase.google.com/
3. Copy your Firebase config into `src/firebaseConfig.js`.
4. Start the app:
   ```
   npm start
   ```

## File Overview
- `src/BookManager.js`: Main UI and logic for managing books
- `src/firebase.js`: Firebase initialization
- `src/models.js`: Data model templates
- `src/App.js`: Renders the book manager UI

---

For any issues, check your Firebase setup and ensure Firestore is enabled.
